      "id": "hook",
      "type": "hook",
      "variant": "question",
      "prompt": "Work out $7^2 - 3^2$. Then work out $(7 + 3) \\times (7 - 3)$. What do you notice?",
      "placeholder": "I notice…"
    },
    {
      "id": "learn",
      "type": "mini_lesson",
      "cards": [
        {
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "A square minus a square",
          "body": "For any two numbers, $a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b)$. So $47^2 - 43^2 = (47 + 43)(47 - 43) = 90 \\times 4 = 360$: no squaring needed."
        },
        {
          "kind": "worked-example",
          "title": "Worked example: 65² − 35²",
          "problem": "Work out $65^2 - 35^2$.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "text": "Add the numbers.",
              "try": {
                "prompt": "What is $65 + 35$?",
                "accepted": ["100"],
                "compute": "65+35"
              }
            },
            {
              "text": "Subtract them: $65 - 35 = 30$.",
              "try": {
                "prompt": "What is $100 \\times 30$?",
                "accepted": ["3000"],
                "compute": "100*30"
              }
            },
            {
              "text": "So $65^2 - 35^2 = 3000$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Why it works",
          "body": "Cut a $b$ by $b$ square from the corner of an $a$ by $a$ square. The L-shape left can be rearranged into a rectangle $(a + b)$ long and $(a - b)$ wide. In algebra: $(a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - ab + ab - b^2 = a^2 - b^2$."
        }
      ]
    },
